  "recap": {
    "headline": "The macro flipped DOVISH (US June CPI 3.5% vs 3.8% exp, -0.4% MoM) while the AI-chip trade cracked again (Meta Compute unwinds the scarcity premium; memory-led KOSPI selloff) - a clean rotation into rate-sensitive value. SMIC (-15% wk) sits at its HK$66 stop and Cambricon broke its ¥1,250 stop; China internet held on a Q2-GDP-miss stimulus put (Alibaba 1-mo turned +5.3%); Thailand stayed the haven (SET>1,600, GULF broke out +6.3% wk). Honor the Cambricon stop, reduce SMIC, rotate into Thai banks/value (KTB, BBL/KBANK) + power-for-AI (GULF/Sembcorp) + Keppel DC REIT; re-engage Alibaba with a starter. Hold powder into the Jul 29 FOMC + megacap earnings.",
    "bullets": [
      "Macro flipped DOVISH: US June CPI (Jul 14) came in at 3.5% YoY vs 3.8% expected and -0.4% MoM (biggest monthly drop since Apr-2020), core just 2.6% on a -5.7% energy decline. Last week's 'hawkish-hold' framing is gone - there's now a genuine rate tailwind for Thai banks/power/REITs and SGX yield into the Jul 29 FOMC.",
      "The AI-chip trade cracked again: 'chip stocks lead selloff as investors question AI assumptions' (Bloomberg Jul 17) - Meta Compute (selling surplus AI capacity) unwinds the scarcity premium and memory (SK Hynix/Samsung) dragged the KOSPI. SMIC fell -15% wk to HK$67.70 (within 2.6% of its HK$66 stop) and Cambricon -15% wk to ¥1,190, through its ¥1,250 stop -> REMOVED.",
      "China Q2 GDP missed at 4.3% (vs 4.5% target, slowest since Q4-2022) but exports +27% and the miss sets up a late-July Politburo stimulus put, so China internet held (Alibaba 1-mo turned +5.3%, re-entry triggered; Tencent +3.6%). Thailand stayed the haven: SET>1,600, ~฿27bn H1 foreign inflows, banks/power led (GULF broke out +6.3% wk). Binary risk: Jul 29 FOMC + megacap earnings (the $725bn AI-capex question)."
